{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>As the breast of the wave-offering and as the thigh of the right side.</b> Of peace-offerings, which are eaten by the priests and their wives, their sons, and their servants for two days and one night — so too the firstborn is eaten for two days and one night." "<b>It shall be yours.</b> Rabbi Akiva comes and teaches: Scripture added for you an extra הֲוָיָה, so that you should not say: like the breast and thigh of the thanksgiving-offering, which is eaten only for a day and a night (Zevachim 57)."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 18, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:11:31.786319456Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}